# Registered exemptions from the host-toolchain policy.
#
# docs/design/build.md section 0 is the policy; tests/host-toolchain-lint.sh is
# what enforces it; this is the list of invocations that break it today and the
# reason each one is still here. An exemption is allowed. An UNEXAMINED path is
# not, and neither is a waiver that outlives what it waived: the lint fails when
# a rule here matches nothing, so a renamed file or a fixed call site turns this
# file red rather than leaving a rule behind about something that is gone.
#
# Format: path<TAB>tool<TAB>reason. One row per (file, tool) pair, not per line.
pkgs/mosd/hack/check.sh	cargo	The Rust gate. The container it needed now EXISTS -- RFCT-309 landed `make os-rust-gate` / tests/rust-gate.sh, which runs this script UNMODIFIED inside localhost/mos-build-rust-check -- so the path is no longer unimplementable. What keeps the row here is .github/workflows/check.yml, which still runs the same script directly on the runner with a rustup toolchain it installs; the script cannot be declared container-side while one of its two callers is a bare host. Comes off with PLAN-080 backlog B7.
pkgs/rauc-sign/hack/check.sh	cargo	The same gate over the second cargo workspace. tests/rust-gate.sh covers it -- it takes both workspaces, which is more than RFCT-309's brief named -- and CI still runs it on the runner, so it stays for B7's reason and not for a missing image.
.github/workflows/check.yml	cargo	The runner that runs the two gates above: it curls rustup and installs a toolchain on the host, which is a host toolchain whoever owns the host. Now that tests/rust-gate.sh exists these steps could become `make os-rust-gate` -- PLAN-080 backlog B7 -- but that makes the runner build the mos-build-* family first, and it is a CI change nothing here can run to prove. Estimated and left.
pkgs/mosd/hack/check.sh	host-toolchain-on-PATH	Line 8 puts $HOME/.cargo/bin in front of PATH, and on a HOST that is the only reason the cargo above resolves: measured 2026-09-04, `command -v cargo` on this container's default PATH answers nothing, while /root/.cargo/bin holds rustup's cargo, rustc 1.98.0, cargo-clippy 0.1.98, cargo-nextest, cargo-deny, rustfmt, miri and audit. Inside localhost/mos-build-rust-check the prepend finds nothing and the image's own PATH answers, which is why tests/rust-gate.sh can run the script unmodified. Comes off with the cargo row above.
pkgs/rauc-sign/hack/check.sh	host-toolchain-on-PATH	Line 13, the same prepend for the same reason over the second workspace. Comes off with its cargo row.
